// DYNAMIC.md §6.5: a `#[test]` fn lowers normally AND registers itself on the
// module-level `__tests` table the runtime walks (§7) — `__tests["name"] = name`.
// No prior case exercised it; no backend emitted the registration.
//
// `main` calls nothing on purpose: the two `#[test]` fns run only because they
// registered on `__tests` and the conformance runtime (§7) walks it in sorted
// name order and invokes each — so the stdout below is produced by the
// registration itself, not by `main`. Delete or mis-key either `__tests[...]`
// line in a golden and that test stops running: stdout diverges, the run-trial
// fails. The ordinary `fn main` gets no entry — registration is gated on the
// attribute.
//
// The Rust anchor has no runtime `__tests` (Rust `#[test]` is compile-time, no
// runtime-observable effect), so it omits the attribute and calls both fns from
// `main` directly to reproduce the same stdout, as the derive cases do.
extern {
    fn println(s: string);
}

#[test]
fn checks_alpha() {
    println("alpha-ran");
}

#[test]
fn checks_beta() {
    println("beta-ran");
}

fn main() {}
